# shell/zinit-uninstall.list — zinit plugins this dotfiles repo used to load
# but no longer does. Read every run by install.sh; each entry is an
# `owner/repo` spec (the same form passed to `zinit light`).
#
# Why this exists: removing a `zinit light X` line from shell/zshrc.local
# stops loading the plugin into the next zsh session, but does NOT clean up
# zinit's plugin cache at ~/.local/share/zinit/plugins/<owner>---<repo>/.
# Adding the spec here makes install.sh do `rm -rf` on the cache the next
# time it runs (idempotent — silent when already absent).
#
# Companion mechanism: dev-bootstrap's lib/uninstall.sh handles the
# brew/apt/clone/binary side of the same retirement (see
# topics/20-terminal-ux/data/uninstall.list). Together they produce a
# clean machine even when both layers had installed the same product.
#
# Format: one `owner/repo` per line. Comments (#) and blank lines ignored.
# Sandbox: entries containing `..` or starting/ending with `/` are rejected.
#
# When deprecating a plugin: ALSO remove the `zinit light` line from
# shell/zshrc.local in the SAME commit. Without the dual edit the plugin
# keeps loading forever on machines already provisioned.

# Removed 2026-04-30: alias-tips already covers the same use case
# (one concise reminder per command), and YSU produced a redundant
# second message per command. Vide PROJECT_STATUS D37.
MichaelAquilina/zsh-you-should-use
